  "id": "dhadi_punjab",
  "name": "Dhadi (Punjabi heroic ballad singing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dhadis are Punjabi ballad singers named after the dhadd, a small hourglass drum struck with the fingers whose pitch is bent by squeezing its lacing; here the hudka card stands in for the dhadd, and the sarangi card for the Punjabi folk sarangi. A dhadi jatha of two dhadd players and a sarangi player sings vars, heroic ballads of Sikh history, at gurdwaras and religious fairs, alternating sung verses with spoken narration, a practice the community traces to the patronage of Guru Hargobind. Sohan Singh Seetal was among its most celebrated twentieth-century singers.",
  "recipe": "classic modern dhadi, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. duet, single lead single track no stacking. hudka uttarakhand, sarangi. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
